<title>FRANCE: ONIC sees EU 96 grain harvest exceeding '91 record.</title>
<headline>ONIC sees EU 96 grain harvest exceeding '91 record.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cereals office ONIC said on Wednesday it expected the European Union grain harvest for 1996 to exceed the 1991 record of 194.8 million tonnes seen before the reform of the CAP.</p>
<p>&quot;We think we should exceed the 1991 record of 194.8 million tonnes,&quot; ONIC director general Alain Moulinier told reporters.</p>
<p>He did, however, emphasise that there were large uncertainties on the European total for cereals. Current estimates were for between 190 and 200 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Estimates for the soft wheat harvest for 1996 were between 88 and 89 million tonnes, versus 80 million in 1995/96, he said.</p>
</text>
